<div class="wrap">
  <header class="head">
    <div class="tag">Vessel import documents · DEMURRAGE</div>
    <div class="brand"><span class="logo-badge"><img class="logo" src="assets/hal-logo.png" alt="Heung A Line"></span><h1>Check DEM</h1></div>
    <p class="lede">Works out the demurrage start date (DEM.) and the container receipt date (REC.) for every B/L from the Freedays and the vessel arrival date (ATA), then produces a CHECK DEM.xlsx report coloured by date, ready to print on A4.</p>
    <div class="flow" aria-label="Workflow">
      <span class="doc">SUR.xls (Freedays)</span><span class="op">+</span>
      <span class="doc">ATA</span><span class="op">→</span>
      <span class="out">CHECK DEM.xlsx</span>
    </div>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn primary" href="../#check-dem">Use online (no install)</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/Rattanao/Check-dem/archive/refs/heads/main.zip">Download the program (ZIP)</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/Rattanao/Check-dem">Open on GitHub</a>
    </div>
    <p class="credit">Project by Ms. Rattana Mudlae · Position Import DOC.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="panel" id="online">
    <h2>Use online</h2>
    <p class="sub">Opens straight in the browser. Files are calculated on the computer you are using only; no data is uploaded anywhere</p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Click "Use online" above</b>, then drag in the Freedays file (.xls / .xlsx) or click to choose it</p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Pick the ATA date</b> and click <b>Calculate</b></p>
        <p class="note">The on-screen table is coloured by DEM. date. Click a date chip to hide or show that date, and search by B/L or Consignee</p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Click "Download CHECK DEM.xlsx"</b></p>
        <p class="note">You get the same Excel file the desktop program produces, saved to your Downloads folder</p>
      </div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="install">
    <h2>Install the desktop program (first time)</h2>
    <p class="sub">Once per computer, Windows. If you use the online tool above, there is nothing to install</p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Install Python 3</b> from <a href="https://www.python.org/downloads/">python.org/downloads</a></p>
        <p class="note">On the installer's first screen <span class="warn">tick ☑ Add python.exe to PATH</span> before clicking Install Now</p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Download the program</b> with the "Download the program (ZIP)" button above</p>
        <p class="note">Right-click the ZIP → Extract All, and keep the folder anywhere, e.g. Documents</p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>The first run needs an internet connection</b></p>
        <p class="note">The program installs the libraries it needs (pandas, openpyxl, xlrd) automatically</p>
      </div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="use">
    <h2>Every job on the desktop</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Put the Freedays file in the <code>input</code> folder</b></p>
        <p class="note">The Excel form can vary; the program finds the headings it needs by name, so there is no need to rearrange columns (see the headings it reads below)</p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Double-click <code>run_check_dem.bat</code></b>, type the ATA date, e.g. <code>04/10/2026</code>, and press Enter</p>
        <p class="note">Always type day/month/year (Gregorian year)</p>
      </div></li>
      <li><div>
        <p><b>Open the result at <code>output\CHECK DEM.xlsx</code></b></p>
        <p class="note">The black window shows the number of B/Ls and how many rows had unreadable Freedays. The file is already set to print A4 portrait, 1 page wide</p>
      </div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="rules">
    <h2>Calculation rules</h2>
    <table class="rules">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>How it is worked out</th><th>Example (ATA 04/10/2026)</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>TOTAL</td><td>First number of Freedays + first number after the word Add</td><td><code>3/3 Add 2/4</code> → 3 + 2 = <b>5</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>DEM.</td><td>ATA + TOTAL days</td><td>04/10/2026 + 5 = <b>09/10/2026</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>REC.</td><td>ATA + 3 days, only on rows with the word TOS or a reefer; other rows are left blank</td><td><code>7/5 Add 7/9 TOS 3</code> → <b>07/10/2026</b></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note"><b>Reefers:</b> if TPSZ starts with R, e.g. <code>R40Hx1</code>, it always counts as TOS 3 because power charges apply. The program fills REC. even when the Freedays cell doesn't say TOS</p>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <h3>Headings the program reads (by name, any position)</h3>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li><b>Freedays</b> (required)</li>
          <li>TPSZ</li>
          <li>B/L No.</li>
          <li>RECEIPT B/L</li>
          <li>Consignee</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Not used</h3>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>All other headings, e.g. POL, STATUS</li>
          <li>The header doesn't have to be in the first row; the program finds the row containing Freedays</li>
          <li>The report always comes out in the same layout, whatever the column order of the source</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="read">
    <h2>Reading the CHECK DEM.xlsx report</h2>
    <p class="sub">One row per B/L. The top row shows the number of B/Ls, the source file name and the ATA date</p>
    <div class="sheet-scroll">
      <table class="sheet">
        <thead>
          <tr class="info"><td class="k">B/L count</td><td class="v">25</td><td></td><td></td><td class="k">Source</td><td class="v b">SUR.xls</td><td></td><td class="k">ATA</td><td class="v b">04/10/2026</td></tr>
          <tr><th>No.</th><th>TPSZ</th><th>REC.</th><th>TOTAL</th><th>Freedays</th><th>DEM.</th><th>B/L No.</th><th>RECEIPT B/L</th><th>Consignee</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1</td><td class="mono">40Hx1</td><td></td><td class="b">14</td><td class="l d2">7/5 Add 7/9</td><td class="b d2">18/10/2026</td><td class="mono">HASLC…0001</td><td class="rcpt">SUR</td><td class="l">ABC LOGISTICS CO.,LTD.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2</td><td class="mono">20'x2</td><td></td><td class="b">21</td><td class="l d3">7/5 Add 14/2</td><td class="b d3">25/10/2026</td><td class="mono">HASLC…0002</td><td class="rcpt"></td><td class="l">TO THE ORDER OF XYZ BANK</td></tr>
          <tr><td>3</td><td class="mono">20TKx1</td><td></td><td class="b"></td><td class="l"></td><td class="bad">CHECK</td><td class="mono">HASLC…0003</td><td class="rcpt">SUR</td><td class="l">DEF TRADING CO.,LTD.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>4</td><td class="mono">R40Hx3</td><td class="recx">07/10/2026</td><td class="b">5</td><td class="l d1 tos">3/3 Add 2/4</td><td class="b d1">09/10/2026</td><td class="mono">HASLC…0004</td><td class="rcpt">SUR</td><td class="l">GHI FOOD CO.,LTD.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>5</td><td class="mono">40Hx1</td><td class="recx">07/10/2026</td><td class="b">5</td><td class="l d1 tos">3/3 Add 2/4 TOS 3</td><td class="b d1">09/10/2026</td><td class="mono">HASLC…0005</td><td class="rcpt">SWB</td><td class="l">JKL SEAFOOD CO.,LTD.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="caption">Illustration only; B/L numbers and company names are made up · Row 4 is a reefer (R40H), so it has a REC. date even though Freedays has no TOS · Row 3 has an empty Freedays cell, so it shows CHECK</p>
    <div class="legend">
      <div class="grad"><b>Colour by DEM. date</b><span>Freedays and DEM. cells with the same date share a colour, from the earliest date (red) to the latest (blue)</span></div>
      <div class="o"><b>Orange (REC. cell)</b><span>Rows with TOS or a reefer: container receipt / power charges apply</span></div>
      <div class="y"><b>Yellow (RECEIPT B/L)</b><span>How the B/L is received, e.g. SUR / SWB, in red text</span></div>
      <div class="r"><b>Red CHECK (DEM. cell)</b><span>Freedays couldn't be read; check and calculate by hand</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="claude">
    <h2>Use with Claude Code</h2>
    <p class="sub">For people who already use Claude Code: let Claude run the program, summarise the results and add rules</p>
    <p>Extract the ZIP, open a command prompt (cmd) in the program folder, and run this to install the skill:</p>
    <div class="cmd">
      <pre id="skill">xcopy /E /I /Y skill\check-dem "%USERPROFILE%\.claude\skills\check-dem"</pre>
      <button type="button" data-target="skill">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <p class="note">Restart Claude Code, go to the job folder, and type e.g. "check dem ATA 04/10/2026"</p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="help">
    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    <div class="trouble-scroll">
      <table class="trouble">
        <thead><tr><th>Message / symptom</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Python not found</td><td>Reinstall Python and tick Add python.exe to PATH</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Python was not found; run without arguments to install from the Microsoft Store</td><td>Windows is sending the python command to the Microsoft Store. Turn it off in Settings → Apps → Advanced app settings → App execution aliases, switching off python.exe and python3.exe</td></tr>
          <tr><td>PermissionError: [Errno 13]</td><td>CHECK DEM.xlsx is open in Excel; close it and run again</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No Freedays heading found in the file</td><td>The source file needs a heading that reads Freedays (or Free Days); check the heading names</td></tr>
          <tr><td>time data ... does not match format</td><td>The ATA was typed in the wrong format; it must be day/month/year, e.g. 04/10/2026</td></tr>
          <tr><td>The DEM. cell shows CHECK</td><td>The Freedays cell is empty or has no number. Check that B/L's Freedays and calculate by hand, or fix the source file and run again</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <p>This report is a calculation aid. Before informing customers, a person must always review every row showing CHECK and the REC. date of every reefer</p>
    <p>Updating the program: download the ZIP again and extract over the old folder (or <code>git pull</code>) · Source code: <a href="https://github.com/Rattanao/Check-dem">github.com/Rattanao/Check-dem</a></p>
  </footer>
</div>
